;; TODO scenarios — the known PROMPT-THIN spots the gym must eventually
;; cover (PRD §7 item 12). Encoded now so the rubric axes have owners;
;; each is :todo because the pass bar needs behavioral (paid) runs and
;; in two cases the TEACHING itself is still too thin to expect a pass:
;;   - test-writing:    thinnest teaching in the current context.
;;   - function-reuse:  never yet observed in any live run.
;;   - store-proactively: storing happens when asked; the default should
;;     be to persist any verified non-trivial result (§2 gap).
;; The driver refuses :todo scenarios — flip :status to :active once the
;; teaching lands and the predicates are sharpened against a live run.
[{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :writes-tests-for-own-fns
  :seon.gym.scenario/competency :planning
  :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "TODO: after defining a fn for the user's task, the agent writes + runs a deftest for it without being asked. Predicate sketch: a :seon.test/sym row exists in the agent's ns AND the test passed. Teaching is currently the thinnest section — expect fail until it lands."
  :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
  :seon.gym.scenario/status :todo
  :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:writes-tests :terminates]
  :seon.gym.scenario/turns
  [{:seon.gym.turn/message "Write a function that converts meters to miles, test it, and store it for reuse."}]
  :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
  [{:seon.gym.predicate/id     :test-row-persisted
    :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
    :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :writes-tests
    :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?t :where [?e :seon.test/sym ?t]]
    :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}]}

